{
 "manufacturer": "Yaskawa",
 "manufacturer_slug": "yaskawa",
 "model": "A1000 AC drive (MEMOBUS/Modbus RTU)",
 "model_slug": "a1000",
 "short_model": "A1000",
 "aliases": [
  "CIMR-AU",
  "CIMR-AUA",
  "A1000 High Performance Vector Control Drive"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
 "applies_to": "Yaskawa A1000 drives (CIMR-AU; 200 V, 400 V and 600 V classes) using the built-in RS-422/485 MEMOBUS/Modbus terminals (TB5), per Technical Manual SIEP C710616 41H.",
 "summary": "Yaskawa's high-performance vector drive with a built-in RS-422/RS-485 MEMOBUS/Modbus RTU port on terminal block TB5. Commands are written to hex registers 0001H-001FH, status, fault and alarm words and key monitors are read from 0020H upwards, and every parameter has its own hex register in the parameter list. This map covers the command block, status/fault/alarm words, the main monitors with fixed units, fault and alarm codes, and the b1/H5 setup parameters.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": 31,
  "baud": 9600,
  "parity": "None",
  "data_bits": 8,
  "stop_bits": 1,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "hex 0-based",
  "note": "Register numbers are printed in hex and go into the request unchanged: the manual's read example asks for starting register 0020H by sending 00 20, and its write example starts at 0001H (00 01). Parameters use the hex address printed under each parameter in the parameter list (H5-01 (0425) -> 0425H, b1-01 (0180) -> 0180H)."
 },
 "default_word_order": null,
 "firmware": "Drive software up to PRG 1021-1024 (per the manual's revision history)",
 "source": {
  "title": "YASKAWA AC Drive-A1000 High Performance Vector Control Drive Technical Manual",
  "doc_number": "SIEP C710616 41H",
  "revision_date": "2022-03",
  "url": "https://www.yaskawa.com/delegate/getAttachment?documentId=SIEPC71061641&cmd=documents&documentName=SIEPC71061641.pdf",
  "pages": "Appendix C pp. 703-734: specifications p. 703, wiring/termination pp. 704-706, H5 setup pp. 707-709, drive control p. 710, timing p. 711, function codes p. 712, message examples pp. 714-715, command data pp. 716-717, monitor data pp. 717-728, broadcast p. 728, fault trace codes pp. 729-730, alarm codes p. 731, Enter command p. 732, error codes p. 733; parameter list b1 p. 561, H5 pp. 616-617, o1-03 p. 636, U monitors pp. 646-652"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Frequency registers (0002H reference, 0023H/0040H U1-01, 0024H/0041H U1-02) use the units chosen in o1-03 (0 = 0.01 Hz, 1 = 0.01% of E1-04, 2 = r/min, 3 = user units); o1-03's default depends on A1-02, so they are left unscaled here.",
  "0042H U1-03 output current is scaled 8192 = drive rated current (U-monitor footnotes); the map converts it to % of rated current.",
  "Left out: 0025H output voltage (unit switched by H5-10; use 0045H), 0026H and 00FBH output current (0.01 A, 0.1 A or 1 A depending on drive model), 0027H/0047H output power (unit not printed in the data table), 0028H/0032H torque reference (sign not stated), 002FH frequency reference bias and 0068H U4-08 heatsink temperature (sign not stated), 003EH/003FH, 0044H and 00ACH-00B8H speed/frequency in r/min and % (sign not stated), 004EH-0050H analog input levels (bipolar inputs, sign not stated), 0007H/0008H FM/AM analog outputs and 001BH-001DH option-card outputs (10 V = 4000H, sign not stated), 00ABH drive rated current (model-dependent units), U4-10/U4-11 kWh, the 0082H-008FH fault-trace snapshot values, and option-card fault words 00D8H-00E4H.",
  "Appendix C labels the ov bit of 0021H, 002AH and 00C0H and code ov in Tables C.6/C.7 'Drive Overheat Warning (ov)'. The manual's own fault and alarm lists (pp. 401, 419, 431) define ov as (DC bus) overvoltage, so this map names it overvoltage and keeps the printed label in brackets.",
  "0022H Data Link Status: bit 1 is reserved and bit 2 has no printed meaning, so only bits 0 and 3-6 are listed.",
  "Values for 0080H/0081H/0090H (U2-01, U2-02, U3-01) and 007FH are the fault and alarm codes of Tables C.6 and C.7 converted from hex to decimal (e.g. 0021H CE = 33).",
  "Appendix C lists reading and writing parameters among the things a master can do over MEMOBUS/Modbus, with the qualifier 'not H5-oo', and its setup steps have H5 entered at the digital operator, so the H5 registers are listed read-only and should be set at the keypad (reading them is not explicitly confirmed either).",
  "Torque registers 0004H/0005H only act when torque control is enabled and the matching 000FH bit is set.",
  "Broadcast (slave address 0) accepts only 0001H, with its own bit layout (bit 0 run, bit 1 direction, bit 4 external fault, bit 5 fault reset, bits C-F terminals S5-S8), and 0002H (30000 = 100%); slaves do not reply."
 ],
